2,Semantic verb classes in Tima (Niger-Congo),https://kups.ub.uni-koeln.de/71144/1/Dissertation_Veit_KUG.pdf,"Tima is a language of the Niger-Congo family spoken in the Nuba mountains in Sudan. The name Tima is an ethnonym used by other communities also living in the Nuba Mountains, as well as by neighbouring Arabic communities.",Tima,Niger-Congo
3,Morphological marking of contrast in Tima,https://laurabecker.gitlab.io/papers/contrast_tima_preprint.pdf,"Abstract Tima (Niger-Congo, Sudan) has two morphological means to express contrast: focus marking and selective marking.",Tima,Niger-Congo
4,(PDF) Morphological marking of contrast in Tima,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/348019957_Morphological_marking_of_contrast_in_Tima,"devices in Tima (Niger-Congo). Based on the Tima data discussed, we argue that contrast, though often closely associated with focus, is an independent phenomenon, as it can be.",Tima,Niger-Congo
5,Chapter 2. Locative expressions and their semantic extensions in Tima,https://www.benjamins.com/catalog/slcs.235.02dim,"Tima (Niger-Congo, Sudan), has three copulae playing a central role in locative expressions. The number-sensitive copulae, ŋkɔ ‘cop:sg’ and ɲcɛ ‘cop:pl’, primarily link two non-verbal phrases.",Tima,Niger-Congo
6,The Nominal and Verbal Morphology of Tima: A Niger-Congo...,https://www.amazon.com/Nominal-Verbal-Morphology-Tima-Niger-Congo/dp/3896455591,"The exact number of Tima speakers is difficult to determine. The most current estimate, based on interviews with native speakers in 2004, is 5,000 (Dimmendaal 2009). Tima is considered as a highly endangered language.",Tima,Niger-Congo
7,(PDF) Homophony and Serial Verbs,https://www.academia.edu/81486042/Homophony_and_Serial_Verbs,"Semantic verb classes in Tima (Niger-Congo), 2023. This study represents a linguistic analysis of verbs in Tima, a Niger-Congo language spoken in Sudan.",Tima,Niger-Congo
8,Studies in African Linguistics,https://uni-freiburg.de/linguistics/wp-content/uploads/sites/380/Roots-of-Ergativity-in-Africa.pdf,"Tima is a Niger-Congo language spoken by around 7000 speakers in the Nuba Mountains of Sudan. Together with Katla and Julut, it forms the group of Katloid languages.",Tima,Niger-Congo
9,An areal typology of kin terms in the Nuba Mountain languages,https://hal.science/hal-04022316/document,"Tima, on its part, stands apart from other Niger-Congo languages of the sample in that it distinguishes five consanguineal generations as it also differentiates between second ascending and second descending generation, without any specification of the sex of the referent.",Tima,Niger-Congo
